WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:19.320
A light so bright that it can't be hidden
Breaks the silence and resurrects in this world

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:30.070
The dry land quakes violently
Sparks clash as we risk our lives

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:37.790
Let a miracle occur, just one more time

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:44.950
The power to regain the pages of memories I lost long ago

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.020
The trusting heart pierces the darkness
Search for the place where the soul rests

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:59.250
The sharp glint in my unblinking eye burns

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:06.700
Two souls - light and shadow
To the future shown in the crystal

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:13.310
Now moving  Overflowing in red  eyes

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.600
My other self will soon begin his search for his lost memories.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:40.620
Your memories from 3,000 years ago is about to come clear.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.690
When that happens, what fate awaits us?

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:51.090
But before we left for Egypt, the God Cards were stolen!

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.260
You’re Bakura!

00:01:54.270 --> 00:02:00.270
Dark Bakura On the Move

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:11.740
You’re...

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.020
Bakura!

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.750
Everyone knows you have the God Cards.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.320
So everyone will try to steal them.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.190
Isn’t it your job to protect them?

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:27.640
Especially against these losers?

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.060
Haga and Ryuzaki!

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.230
You're so pathetic!  Take 'em!

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.110
The cards are safe.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.040
But...

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:44.740
You mean this?

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:49.120
I'll hold on to it as a reward.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.980
It belongs to me anyway.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.420
I see.  You're his dark side.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.520
But don’t worry.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:02.770
When the Pharaoh regains his memories, he’ll need all the Millennium Items.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:06.100
When that time comes, I'll give this back.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:11.060
How much does Bakura know about the Millennium Items?

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.600
The tablet of the Pharaoh’s memories is in an underground temple in Egypt.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.780
It has spaces to insert the Millennium Items.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.710
Bakura, do you know what'll happen...

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:29.020
...if the seven Millennium Items are placed in the stone tablet?

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.160
Are you talking about the tablet of memories in Kul Elna Village?

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:40.110
That tablet is an ancient artifact that connects this world with the next.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.040
Connect this world with the next?

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:49.480
When the seven Millennium Items are placed in the tablet, the door to the afterlife opens.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.760
Door to the afterlife?

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:59.290
Behind that door is my real target.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:05.220
Do you understand what opening the door to the afterlife signifies?

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:14.670
I do.  My other self- I mean, the Pharaoh's soul inside the Puzzle will return to the afterlife.

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:16.740
Exactly.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:22.840
That is your mission, and I'll help you fulfill it.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:25.840
Bakura, what are you...

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.290
Bakura!  What are you planning!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.340
The Pharaoh showed up.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.680
Worried that I’ll trick your vessel?

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.170
Answer me, Bakura!

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:43.560
Don’t be so cold.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:49.610
I’m a soul who was sealed away 3,000 years ago, just like you.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.040
Who are you really?

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.710
Who knows.  I’ve forgotten myself.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.980
But I might know if I’m inside your memories.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.410
Bakura...

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:04.430
Why don’t we settle things once and for all, Pharaoh?

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:09.800
At a location best suited for both of us – in the world of your memories.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.870
The world of my memories?

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.860
You don’t know anything about yourself.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:23.310
Your heart is a maze, and you're surrounded by games full of mysteries.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:29.000
But the source of your mysteries is the world of your memories.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:32.740
Where lies the ultimate Shadow Game!

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:35.200
Ultimate Shadow Game?

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:40.740
You probably don’t remember, but you're the one who started the game.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.060
I started the Shadow Game?

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:45.980
That’s why we’ll end things there.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:50.940
The world of my memories is the ultimate Shadow Game...

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.360
Fine, Bakura!  I accept your challenge!

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.360
That’s the spirit.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.320
The game begins when you open the door to your memories.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.240
I’m looking forward to it.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:11.480
There's still something I must do.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:15.980
I need to prepare in order to win the ultimate Shadow Game.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:28.860
What's going on?

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:35.790
What's up, President?

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.680
Working overtime?

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.110
You’re Bakura!

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.490
Mokuba!

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.150
Don’t worry.  He’s just unconscious.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.590
You punk!  What do you want!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:52.250
I just came to say hello.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:55.470
I want you to experience a Shadow Game with me.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.570
Let’s duel, Master Seto.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:24.720
Mokuba!

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.160
Took you long enough.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:31.160
Let’s start the Shadow Game.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:34.380
Shadow Game?  How lame.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:37.160
How dare you hurt Mokuba!

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.610
Your luck has run out.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.840
You won't leave unpunished.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.120
That’s the spirit.

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:47.130
You’ll regret this.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:52.150
Here I go!

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.510
Duel!

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:04.960
Why’s the air so heavy?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.050
Don’t be surprised.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:11.400
You also experienced this game many times 3,000 years ago.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.800
A 3,000 year-old game?

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:18.270
As I travel the road to the future, my past glories lead to today’s victory.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:21.560
Save your lame occult jokes for Yugi!

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:27.250
By the way, Yugi will also participate in my Shadow Game.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.190
What?

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:31.910
The ultimate Shadow Game awaits for me and Yugi.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:36.200
So I need some insurance.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:43.610
Your deck has the only monster that can oppose the Gods.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:47.200
I'm going first!  I draw!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:52.000
I fuse Headless Knight and The Earl of Demise from my hand!

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.280
I summon The Duke of Demise!

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.690
The player who goes first can't attack.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.320
I end my turn.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:09.040
You summoned a monster with 2000 attack points on your first turn.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.830
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:13.210
Come forth, Vorse Raider!

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:20.080
That doesn’t have enough attack points.

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:21.810
Don’t be impatient.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:26.090
I activate the spell card, Shrink from my hand!

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:29.340
A monster's attack points are halved!

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.360
Go, Vorse Raider!

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.880
Your monster can't be destroyed in battle.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:45.870
So I'll pummel you to death instead.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:49.300
Go ahead and try.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:51.730
I end my turn.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.020
My turn!

00:09:54.020 --> 00:10:00.740
Due to your monster, you lose 500 life points every time it’s your turn.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.580
Lose them now.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:06.440
You know all the annoying details!

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:11.650
I tribute The Duke of Demise to summon Diabound Kernel.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:17.450
I activate the Equip Spell, Spirit Illusion from my hand.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:24.330
It Special Summons a Doppler Token with the same stats as the equipped monster.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:28.260
It's no problem how many weaklings you summon.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.340
Are you sure?

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:33.270
Go, Doppler Diabound!

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:35.200
What?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.880
Doppler Diabound has an effect.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:47.150
By possessing a monster, it loses attack points equal to Doppler Diabound's.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:51.990
Now your monster only has 100 attack points.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.870
Take this, Seto!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.580
I set one card and end my turn!

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:08.510
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.440
I summon Lord of D.!

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.320
Lord of D.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:22.570
As long as it's faceup, spells and traps can't target Dragons.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:26.920
Then I activate the spell card, The Flute of Summoning Dragon!

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:33.880
When Lord of D. is on the field, I can summon two Dragons from my hand!

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:42.140
Come out, my beautiful, strongest servant!

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:44.780
Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:49.330
The dragon with blue eyes has finally appeared.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.120
The only monster that can oppose the Gods.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.790
What did I just see?

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.170
The two Gods' attack points are the same!

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:46.740
What?

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:22.410
What...

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:26.250
...is this?

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:42.330
The fog covered the town.  How gloomy.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:49.440
It's the same vision Yugi and I saw when our two Gods clashed.

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:53.370
What’s wrong?  It’s your turn!

00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:01.250
My priority is to defeat you, not think about a stupid vision!

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:04.190
Here I go!  Blue-Eyes attacks!

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.120
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.030
It won't work.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:11.560
My trap card, Spirit Shield!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:14.660
What?

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.960
Too bad.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:26.410
By removing a Fiend or Zombie in my graveyard from play, Spirit Shield negates your attack.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:32.050
I can keep using this effect, as long as I have monsters in my graveyard to pay this cost.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.980
So I'll be safe for awhile.

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.720
That won't last forever!

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:39.360
I set one card.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.280
I end my turn.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:47.670
If I don’t find a way to destroy it, I can't fulfill my goal.

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:52.100
I activate the spell card, Pot of Greed from my hand.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:56.810
It lets me add two cards to my hand.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:59.480
Then I activate this spell card!

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:01.360
Grief Tablet!

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:06.410
Lord of D.!

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:13.350
The monster trapped inside the tablet has its effects sealed away.

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:18.170
In order to break the spell, you have to destroy it yourself.

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:22.760
But if you do, you’ll take 500 points of damage.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:28.740
Now Doppler Token, possess Blue-Eyes!

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:35.340
Blue-Eyes!

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:38.180
Go, Diabound Kernel!

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.240
Death Spiral!

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:43.050
I activate my trap, Attack Guidance Armor!

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:52.790
It survived.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:56.740
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:59.080
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:03.750
He has thoroughly analyzed my deck.

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.850
But the true king will win!

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:08.680
That’s why I have my deck!

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:11.030
That’s why I have Blue-Eyes!

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:15.080
I activate the spell card, Card of Demise from my hand!

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:18.160
I draw until I have five cards in my hand.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.190
And discard my entire hand five turns later.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:27.720
No matter what card you draw, I have my invincible Spirit Shield.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:30.130
Then I'll destroy that shield!

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:33.140
The spell card, Soul Release!

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:38.510
It removes The Earl of Demise and The Duke of Demise in your graveyard from play!

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:43.950
You no longer have Fiends or Zombies in your graveyard!

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:46.950
So your Shield is also gone!

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:53.560
I activate the spell card, Silent Doom from my hand!

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:57.170
I summon Vorse Raider from my graveyard in defense position!

00:16:57.170 --> 00:17:01.000
Then I tribute Vorse Raider and Blue-Eyes.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.150
Forgive me, but I can’t see you like this.

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:06.700
So be reborn!

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.710
Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:16.580
He tributed his Blue-Eyes to summon a new Blue-Eyes!

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:20.520
You'll never defeat my Blue-Eyes!

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:23.790
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:28.840
Impressive.

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:30.650
But it's not over!

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.690
I activate my trap, Mirror Tablet!

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.940
And another trap, Rebirth Tablet!

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:44.880
What?

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:49.950
The trap card, Rebirth Tablet activates when a monster is destroyed.

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:53.470
It revives one monster from my graveyard.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:54.820
And then...

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:05.460
Due to Mirror Tablet, when a monster is destroyed...

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:09.420
...half that monster’s attack points are added to mine.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:12.700
And you're forced to battle that monster.

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:16.660
Now Diabound Kernel has more attack points than yours!

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:20.310
Go, Diabound Kernel!

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:21.900
Death Spiral!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.980
Blue-Eyes is immortal!

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:31.990
The spell card, Monster Reborn!

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:38.300
Good.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:45.700
Diabound's true power is that it can absorb the effects of the monsters it destroys.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.700
I’ve fulfilled my goal.

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:54.980
Look at the time.

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:59.420
Unfortunately, I'll have to cut this short.

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.850
What?  You’re quitting this duel?

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:06.700
I have to go on a little trip.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.790
You hold on to this!

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:11.200
This is...

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:26.070
Pegasus’s...

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:28.470
Yes.  The Millennium Eye.

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:31.740
It's an invitation to the ultimate Shadow Game.

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:37.100
If you want to settle things between us, bring it with you to Egypt.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:39.200
Egypt?  Whatever!

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:43.680
I told you I’m not interested in occult items!

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:48.630
But aren’t you interested in your connection with Blue-Eyes?

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:51.620
Me and Blue-Eyes?

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:55.080
I’ll be waiting, Seto.

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:14.150
My connection with Blue-Eyes...

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.460
Hey!

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.280
Yugi!

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:39.520
Huh?  Jonouchi, Anzu, Honda?

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:40.780
What’s with the bags?

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.000
Should be obvious!

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.220
We’re going to Egypt too!

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:47.030
But...

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:49.310
Don't worry about the airfare.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.230
Anzu paid for it!

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.840
Wait a sec, Jonouchi!

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:55.670
I'm only letting you borrow my savings!

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.960
I know.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.870
I'll get a part-time job and pay you back.

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:03.600
I begged my sister for money.

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:08.060
Basically, there’s no way we won't see him off.

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:11.420
Because the other Yugi is our friend too!

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:12.540
Exactly!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:14.480
Thank you, everyone!

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:17.180
We're going to Egypt together!

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:24.540
The world of my memories will finally be opened.

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:33.520
And that’s when the ultimate Shadow Game between me and Bakura begins.

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:16.730
Right now, we don't need a map

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:32.450
The miracle that tore through the darkness is in my hand

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:38.290
Without a goal in mind

00:22:39.610 --> 00:22:46.860
We just step towards our dream

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:52.500
EYE'S  As you sense it

00:22:52.690 --> 00:23:00.970
Your eye will find it

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:06.780
Oh! EYE'S  What you wish for

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:14.920
Will touch your soul

00:23:15.110 --> 00:23:18.180
In a duel

00:23:27.980 --> 00:23:30.980
Of course we're going to Egypt!

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:35.930
There's no way we won't see the other Yugi off!

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:40.210
Because the other Yugi might still...

00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:42.780
No, I can't feel sad!

00:23:42.780 --> 00:23:46.970
It's what he wants, so I should send him off with a smile.

00:23:46.970 --> 00:23:52.650
Ishizu awaits us in Egypt, and she takes us to the tablet of memories.

00:23:52.650 --> 00:23:55.460
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
The Door of Memories Opens

00:23:55.460 --> 00:23:56.770
Stay tuned!
